    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133">

                <pb facs="0318" n="270" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg270"/>

                <head>No. 133.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Sir Edward Thornton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-03-03"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 3,
                        1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of the 27th January
                    last, with which you forwarded to me certain articles and stores belonging to
                    the Polaris expedition which had been recovered by Her Majesty’s ships Alert and
                    Discovery during their explorations in the Arctic Sea, I have the honor to
                    inclose herewith a copy of a letter dated the 2d instant, which has been
                    received from the Secretary of the Navy, expressing the thanks of his department
                    for the collection of these objects and their return to the United States.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d133-a1.xml" xpointer="d133-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
